'''Chatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Uddanpul''' is in [[Nashik]] city, Dwarka area. It starts from Pandavleni caves and ends near Adgaon. It is India's first externally-strutted segmental box girder bridge. it has capacity of 100 [[Ton]] each<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ultratechcement.com/project_pimpalgaon.php |title=UltraTech Cement Limited &#124;&#124; Projects &#124;&#124; PimpalGaon-Nashik-Gonde Road Project |publisher=Ultratechcement.com |date= |accessdate=2013-07-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130527011545/http://www.ultratechcement.com/project_pimpalgaon.php |archive-date=27 May 2013 |url-status=dead }}</ref> and India's second-longest road bridge. It was approved by [[Atal Bihari Vajpayee]] in 2002.

